{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-4 results are all scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile, with transformer aggregation and weighted fusion (config_050, 0.7250) as the best. All four aggregation×fusion combinations for this encoder pair have been tested, so no further gain is expected within that subspace. The remaining untested scvi_n200 + vit_l configurations are the singleprofile variants (config_010, config_027), which remove the aggregation step entirely. Question: This experiment tests whether the multiprofile + transformer architecture is truly necessary or whether a simpler singleprofile pipeline with the same strong encoders (scvi_n200, vit_l) and weighted fusion could be competitive—potentially at lower cost. Rationale: As the final experiment, config_010 is the most logical extension of our best finding (same encoders, same fusion preference), it is the only untested variant in the proven-best encoder space, and it is expected to be relatively cheap (~3–4 GPU hours, no aggregation step) compared to the multiprofile configs. It is very unlikely to beat 0.7250, but it provides the cleanest confirmation that multiprofile + transformer aggregation is the key architectural advantage, and it keeps total GPU hours low. No other untested configuration has a realistic chance of exceeding the current best."
}

